Return a value from ssem_trywait.

    rsemaphore.c:104:7: error: 'return' with no value, in function returning
    non-void [-Wreturn-mismatch]

The null check in a bool function returns nothing. GCC has warned about this
for years and made it an error by default in 14, so the core stopped
building against the current devkitA64 (15.2.0) while remaining fine on
whatever the buildbot pins.

false is the only defensible value: a semaphore that does not exist has not
been acquired, and every caller treats the result as "did I get it".

diff --git a/src/libretro/libretro-common/rthreads/rsemaphore.c b/src/libretro/libretro-common/rthreads/rsemaphore.c
index 7d32524..523d001 100644
--- a/src/libretro/libretro-common/rthreads/rsemaphore.c
+++ b/src/libretro/libretro-common/rthreads/rsemaphore.c
@@ -101,7 +101,7 @@ void ssem_wait(ssem_t *semaphore)
 bool ssem_trywait(ssem_t *semaphore)
 {
    if (!semaphore)
-      return;
+      return false;
 
    slock_lock(semaphore->mutex);
 
